# 🔀 Git Merge :
git merge is used to combine the changes from one branch into another branch.

If you want to merge feature into main:
git switch main
git merge feature

# Why Do We Need Git Merge?

In a real project, developers normally don't work directly on main.

For example:
main
 │
 ├── feature/login
 ├── feature/payment
 ├── feature/search
 └── bugfix/database

Each developer works independently.
Eventually, their changes need to be combined into the main codebase.
That's where git merge is used.

feature/login
      │
      ↓
    merge
      │
      ↓
     main


